{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d","id":153267,"title":"Sidereals As \u201cPrepared Casters\u201d","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-29T17:17:39-07:00","id":153267,"title":"Sidereals As \u201cPrepared Casters\u201d","content":"This concept came up in a discussion about how the celestial splats can be balanced against each while still maintaining the concept of Solars being the best at what they do in a very straight forward sense of achievement. We were trying to come up with roundabout ways in which the other splats can work around or, even negate the power a solar gains from just \u201cbeing better\u201d than everyone else.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not super familiar with the Sidereal charm set so this concept might already be represented in some way, but I am pretty sure there aren't charms that function exactly this way. What if by committing motes a Sidereal could craft fortuitous destinies and hold them in reserve until they were in need of them. For example the Sidereal could envision a destiny where they dodge a mighty blow and make a stinging counter attack, then tuck that destiny away. Later in a fight against a solar where the momentum of the fight is very much against them, their motes are running low, and they have a few bad wounds, they could pull out the destiny they made in the image of their peak performance and hope to turn the fight around. These would be charms that were most effective when prepared ahead of time, perhaps costing a surcharge of motes or even paradox when used on the fly.<br /> <br /> Another thought revolving around manipulating fragments of destiny was the thought of a Sidereal stealing the good fate surrounding an enemy\u2019s actions and giving them to an ally to use. For example the Sidereal senses that Solar is about to make a devastating motion in a meeting of lords, so he steals the good fortune surrounding this action, and gives it to his ally. The Solar finds his argument suddenly fall flat, and the person across the table from him suddenly puts forward a stunning rebuke\u2026in a way that strangely reminds him of something he would say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T17:53:10-07:00","id":153326,"title":"","content":"Interesting thought experiment. I think you'd need to be careful that a Sidereal caught without prep (or without someone else's success to piggyback) isn't made <i>too</i> helpless. I like to think of Sidereal powers as flexible plot devices that, with a little bit of effort, the Sidereal can make fit a whole range of situations. You maneuver in real time to line up your &quot;shots&quot;, like figuring out how to tell your target the opposite of what you want him to think before dropping Avoiding the Truth Technique. To me that's what feeds their &quot;secret agent&quot; vibe and more generally makes their idiosyncratic powers actually fun to play with in the game.<br /> <br /> In comparison you seem to be suggesting that they instead get the broadly-applicable power to fabricate special-case powers in advance. In my mind that turns them into gadgeteers, something more like Q than 007. That is, something more like a D&amp;D Wizard (obviously intentional, from your title). Being caught with your pants down because you didn't prep the right power doesn't suit Heaven's elite troubleshooters very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 05-29-2014, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T18:00:09-07:00","id":153331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=153326#post153326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting thought experiment. I think you'd need to be careful that a Sidereal caught without prep (or without someone else's success to piggyback) isn't made <i>too</i> helpless. I like to think of Sidereal powers as flexible plot devices that, with a little bit of effort, the Sidereal can make fit a whole range of situations. To me that's what feeds their &quot;secret agent&quot; vibe and more generally makes their idiosyncratic powers actually fun to play with in the game. In comparison you seem to be suggesting that they instead get the broadly-applicable power to fabricate special-case powers in advance. In my mind that turns them into something more like Q than 007. That is, something more like a D&amp;D Wizard (obviously intentional, from your title). But D&amp;D Wizards make poor individual operators; they're better off hanging out at the back behind the meat shields. Being helpless when the fire elemental attacks because all you prepared that day was fireballs doesn't strike me as very Sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this mechanic would entirely replace how they function right now, it would more be like a subset or style of charms that could be found scattered across the abilities where applicable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T18:49:11-07:00","id":153361,"title":"","content":"The biggest issue with sidereals is that their schtick is intrinsically linked to being ST NPCs.<br /> <br /> Sidereals essentially mesh Burn Notice, Person of Interest and Kung Fu the Legend Continues all into one character type. All of which hinge on the concept that they function with ST level knowledge of the setting as to what is currently happening and what will happen. It might be simpler just to make Sidereals an explicitly ST only territory, rather than a player choice.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are by definition supposed to operate Xanatos Gambits as a default. But if you try to make that into a mechanic you wind up with things like Shards of Obsidian style final charm which is essentially choosing to use a given fate based outcome.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you make it just a question of backgrounds which can be used as tools, the whole thing hinges upon the abilities of the player to connect the dots. This leads to the scenario where people do white room simulations and &quot;prove&quot; that the splat is under powered because there is no direct mechanics to prove supremacy..... or you get players like me who look at all the toys and start grinning. I mean how much damage can my character do by just saying he was an architect during his mortal life and has an interest in geomancy? But then that is considered broken because once again no direct, simple rock-paper-scissors mechanic to counter such a play style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T18:52:54-07:00","id":153363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=153361#post153361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest issue with sidereals is that their schtick is intrinsically linked to being ST NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only do I disagree with this, I reject it.<br /> <br /> The name of the game is &quot;Exalted.&quot; Not &quot;Solar Exalted,&quot; not &quot;Dragon-Blooded Exalted.&quot; If something is - by its nature - unplayable? It shouldn't be a type of Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T18:53:08-07:00","id":153364,"title":"","content":"Personally I favor &quot;oh yeah, this is totally what I prepared when you weren't looking&quot; powers over fire-and-forget wizardry, for three reasons:<ul><li>First, fire-and-forget wizardry is based on an annoying dance of having to read the ST's mind and the ST having to work to ensure some but not all of your preparations are actually useful. Break the plan too often and the Sidereal feels cheated, don't break it and the campaign's boring.</li> <li>Second, it puts too much onus on the intellect of the player over the intellect of the character. It's good to challenge the player's intellect, but their Sidereal is almost certainly supposed to be better at this than the player is, and the player is equally good at planning regardless of if they're playing a Sidereal or a Solar.</li> <li>Third, and maybe most importantly, retroactive preparation puts the Sidereals on the winning side of their narrative. Almost any time a plan is prepared for on-camera in fiction, it means it's going to fail. Any time a plan is prepared for on-camera in a game, there's going to be something that happens partway through that makes the entire plan blow up. Fictional plans work when we the audience don't see exactly how they were set up, or were shown some of the steps but didn't have the actual plan pointed out to us, and similarly plans in a game have to be made without the ST's awareness or you can practically guarantee they're going to fail. Giving Sidereals the ability to have had a plan all along makes them Nate Ford revealing the victory twist at the end, demanding that they plan out everything in advance and in view of the ST makes them Hannibal from the A-Team creating the plan that doesn't work...which only works because the planners are actually very good at <i>improvisation</i>, which is the <i>opposite</i> of what you want to convey with powers that demand extensive real-life planning.</li> </ul>Fire-and-forget wizardry primarily leaves D&amp;D wizards on top because D&amp;D wizards are <i>hilariously overpowered</i> for the setting and game system that they're in, and simple preparations legitimately leave them at zero risk of anything except another spellcasting-capable creature being an actual threat to them. It doesn't work for Sidereals because they're not on top of the power heap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","user":"Couch","date":". 05-29-2014, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T19:30:04-07:00","id":153399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=153363#post153363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only do I disagree with this, I reject it.<br /> <br /> The name of the game is &quot;Exalted.&quot; Not &quot;Solar Exalted,&quot; not &quot;Dragon-Blooded Exalted.&quot; If something is - by its nature - unplayable? It shouldn't be a type of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are entirely free to reject it, but it doesn't change the fact that bad game design doesn't magically go away if all one does is change the window dressing, but still keep the same flawed core intact.<br /> <br /> The problem with prepared casters is that after a certain point they are dependent on foreknowledge and will actively avoid any situation where they can't have it. This automatically limits role playing and character mechanics. Playing a prepared caster without said foreknowledge is basically agreeing to be in a combat focused game with no combat charms in your load out, let alone critical things like perfect defenses.<br /> <br /> On the flip side of the coin, if you are given said foreknowledge, then how do you balance that against the other classes? If I know there is going to be a battle at such a place in the future, I don't show up to it, I place a bomb under it and detonate it days later when everyone else is focused on their declarations of blood &amp; honor. But that means you have invalidated the functionality of the other character builds. The ST can attempt to counter this with story based contrivance, but after a certain point it gets rather ridiculous how often this becomes a restriction. <br /> <br /> It's like having an ST who traps every single door, chest, floor tile and toilet paper roll. It is almost impossible to stop because the foreknowledge character doesn't show up to deal with things directly. Thus all those shiny mega-damage combos don't do any good.<br /> <br /> What usually happens next is that the game design attempts to add the appearance of being a prepared caster with fluff, but uses mechanics that only work within specific scenarios such as combat. But that in truth isn't controlling fate, that is just another way to stunt or use a standard charm with a face lift.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T20:09:00-07:00","id":153423,"title":"","content":"Actually, if you read through the charm set, alot of their charms do function like sorcery spells, by which I mean, some of them bind spirits, some of them banish spirits, some move cities. In alot of ways, Sidereal charms in 2e make them the sort of &quot;fast cast&quot; option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T20:23:42-07:00","id":153442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=153423#post153423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, if you read through the charm set, alot of their charms do function like sorcery spells, by which I mean, some of them bind spirits, some of them banish spirits, some move cities. In alot of ways, Sidereal charms in 2e make them the sort of &quot;fast cast&quot; option.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e even moreso. It's almost like they were designed that way on purpose, and that all that fluff that predates their book describing them as great sorcerers wasn't total bull if you consider the splat as a whole rather than just what Circle they can reach.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T20:33:20-07:00","id":153450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=153364#post153364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I favor &quot;oh yeah, this is totally what I prepared when you weren't looking&quot; powers over fire-and-forget wizardry, for three reasons:</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Drifter Panoply is quite possibly one of the best Charms ever written for the game. If 3e Sidereals don't have a &quot;contemporary&quot; version of it, I will be sorely disappoint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d#post153267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thought revolving around manipulating fragments of destiny was the thought of a Sidereal stealing the good fate surrounding an enemy\u2019s actions and giving them to an ally to use. For example the Sidereal senses that Solar is about to make a devastating motion in a meeting of lords, so he steals the good fortune surrounding this action, and gives it to his ally. The Solar finds his argument suddenly fall flat, and the person across the table from him suddenly puts forward a stunning rebuke\u2026in a way that strangely reminds him of something he would say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they can sorta do that now with Sidereal Shell Games, but I wouldn't be opposed to seeing something like that in the updated version.<br /> <br /> ...and to think that I thought I would have to come into this thread and threaten to beat people to death with a tuna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T21:13:01-07:00","id":153465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=153399#post153399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are entirely free to reject it, but it doesn't change the fact that bad game design doesn't magically go away if all one does is change the window dressing, but still keep the same flawed core intact.<br /> <br /> The problem with prepared casters is that after a certain point they are dependent on foreknowledge and will actively avoid any situation where they can't have it. This automatically limits role playing and character mechanics. Playing a prepared caster without said foreknowledge is basically agreeing to be in a combat focused game with no combat charms in your load out, let alone critical things like perfect defenses.<br /> <br /> On the flip side of the coin, if you are given said foreknowledge, then how do you balance that against the other classes? If I know there is going to be a battle at such a place in the future, I don't show up to it, I place a bomb under it and detonate it days later when everyone else is focused on their declarations of blood &amp; honor. But that means you have invalidated the functionality of the other character builds. The ST can attempt to counter this with story based contrivance, but after a certain point it gets rather ridiculous how often this becomes a restriction.<br /> <br /> It's like having an ST who traps every single door, chest, floor tile and toilet paper roll. It is almost impossible to stop because the foreknowledge character doesn't show up to deal with things directly. Thus all those shiny mega-damage combos don't do any good.<br /> <br /> What usually happens next is that the game design attempts to add the appearance of being a prepared caster with fluff, but uses mechanics that only work within specific scenarios such as combat. But that in truth isn't controlling fate, that is just another way to stunt or use a standard charm with a face lift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I disagree to some extent. A prepared caster should resemble something closer to Alchemicals. Which is what I've been advocating for Astrology for the longest time. You think you have to go to war you give yourself a destiny of a great Soldier and gain benefits for it. You think you need to be social diplomat you cover your destiny with that a person who could sell anyone sand. Creating a Destiny that takes time and effort while boosting your abilities and giving you what are essentially resplendencies to cover your deficiencies. If you prepare a soldier's destiny but don't get into a fight and have to negotiate it's unfortunate but sidereals aren't ultimate prophets and alchemicals can get away with wrong loadouts all the time even though it sucks for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T03:40:15-07:00","id":153639,"title":"","content":"Actually that's kinda like the resplendency powers they already have.<br /> For instance there is a resplendency that makes you ignore fatigue penalties for a task and instead treat them as bonus dice. That's a very good tool in a situation where you want to challenge someone in arm-wrestling. Combined with sidereal shell-games it's very easy to defeat stronger opponents when you're prepared.<br /> <br /> these power can really make a huge difference and they need prior planing since they take hours, if not days, to create a resplendent destiny. And since you're limited to (essence) destinies, you can't just activate all of them.You have to choose which powers you will be using. So it totally fits what you are advocating.<br /> <br /> They are even more interesting because they cost nothing in terms of &quot;normal&quot; resources (motes, wp, health levels). That gives even more advantages if choose them wisely. I think the only thing needed is having powers covering a bit more diverse options. Some are quite redundant and the themes they cover are limited. Also some powers are totally &quot;generic&quot; like accelerate willpower recovery, travel faster. Specific powers like &quot;instantly createa talisman&quot; or summon arrows that bring outside-of-fate creature inside are much cooler and would fit more situations where you have a plan or somehow know in advance about what's about to come.<br /> <br /> But there are a few issues for them to be practical :<br /> - when you create a destiny, duration and endurance are in competition but the destiny ends when either the duration is finished or you use the last endurance dot.<br /> - The role of the destiny can get stuck between the identity and the usefulness the the resplendencies. If you do meaningful things with the identity and need to keep it (if you get a position of authority through that identity) you're screwed. Especially since you can have only one destiny for each college.<br /> - you can't &quot;refill&quot; the destiny's endurance dots or increase its duration either<br /> - the main ressource used, endurance, is fixed for each destiny. You can't use a destiny in a specific college to fuel resplendencies in another college<br /> <br /> A few changes are required to make the system less painful. Either :<br /> - Remove the &quot;duration&quot; trait for destinies. They last as long as you haven't used the last endurance dot<br /> <br /> - Make both uses independent : destinies only have a duration trait and will last until the end. Endurance dots are gathered in another way and do not impact the destinies, and they possibly are a &quot;global&quot; ressource not tied to a particular college.<br /> <br /> - Allow cross-colleges use of endurance dots, but you still require an active destiny in the college to use its powers. That way you can have one or two &quot;trash&quot; destinies that exist only to fuel your resplendencies, and you keep your important identities safe from disappearing due to endurance depletion.<br /> <br /> - Allow for a method to replenish endurance or move it from a destiny to the other.<br /> <br /> TL; DR :<br /> <br /> Resplendencies have the ability to cover what you need, just tweak how you pay endurance and change a few &quot;boring&quot; powers to make them fill gaps in the sidereals' charmset and it will be perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T04:46:50-07:00","id":153701,"title":"","content":"Resplendencies don't. They are minor benefits as is. That fatigue charm is already beaten by Resistance most of those abilities aren't nearly as powerful as you'd need them to be to make astrology worth wild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T05:39:24-07:00","id":153722,"title":"","content":"If you mean that it's beaten by a resistance charm that :<br /> - requires 9/11 XP and has as prerequisite another resistance charm (another 9/11 xp)<br /> - costs 8 motes 1 willpower<br /> - only allows you to ignore the penalties, not convert them into bonus dice (uncapped because not from charms)<br /> <br /> Yes maybe.<br /> <br /> Personally, I see a clear advantage using the resplendency and not risk spending motes, willpower, and potentially revealing a caste mark/flaring anima etc...<br /> Also they're pretty cheap, XP-wise : the 1st dot of a college is 2/3 xp depending if it's caste/favored, and it gives you access to 3 resplendencies.<br /> <br /> Also there is countless other situational advantages, like :<br /> <br /> - not being detected by essence-vision<br /> <br /> - in 2E rules, they completely bypass the combo limitations<br /> <br /> - slipping through charm restriction powers. For instance the artifact manacles that prevent the use of charms doesn't prevent a sidereal from turning into a crow and fly away, instantly kill a mortal with tears of the blade or activate everywhere and nowhere technique to escape the prison cell whenever at the first moment you're not looking at him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T05:41:52-07:00","id":153740,"title":"","content":"That doesn't mean they worth-wild they especially don't merit an investment in astrology to acquire them as they are. There are better ways to get around the manacles than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T06:35:48-07:00","id":153791,"title":"","content":"better than an investment of 2 or 3 XP, and costs less than 0 motes 0 willpower, 3 paradox dice?<br /> <br /> 3 paradox dice = approx 1.5 paradox points.<br /> Those points naturally disappear at a rate of 1 each 3 month which means that unless you count on using it more frequently than once every 4 month and a half (statistically) you're having it free.<br /> <br /> I mean, even some lunars can be jaleous since it costs no mote, can be used at whatever anima banner level without handicap.<br /> <br /> I'ld be seriously impressed by any better way to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T14:33:54-07:00","id":154180,"title":"","content":"You can slip them off as soon as they get put on with a charm. Even though it's free everywhere and nowhere doesn't remove anything from your person so you'd still have them on. You'd escape though furthermore what I'm asking for is a system that would let astrology worth actually investing in. As is most of those powers are more like parlor tricks rather than strong effects there are random exceptions but it's few and far between. The one major problem with everywhere and nowhere is that it literally forces you to be removed from the campaign for a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T21:14:19-07:00","id":154506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=153363#post153363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only do I disagree with this, I reject it.<br /> <br /> The name of the game is &quot;Exalted.&quot; Not &quot;Solar Exalted,&quot; not &quot;Dragon-Blooded Exalted.&quot; If something is - by its nature - unplayable? It shouldn't be a type of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and No! Even the current 3E designers have said that the &quot;story of Exalted is the return of the Solars&quot;. Now just because that's the big schtick of the story, doesn't mean you shouldn't be able to play other Exalted though. The game has allow play of many types (mortal, terrestrial, raksha, celestial exalts, etc) since 1st edition. There's absolutely no reason, and no intent by the current designers to change that. As for Sidereals, they may need a bit more ST assistance then others. But their Astrology exists for that very reason. It gives them a way of tapping into the ST and pulling tid bits of info from the source. While I've never cared much for Sidereals myself, I always thought clever uses of astrology were some of the most interesting reasons to play a Sidereal.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I think people just need to wait for their 3E splat book. Useless speculation on Sidereals, Lunars, Infernals, or whatever really, is pointless. Outside of the designers themselves, none of us know how things will change. Speculation based on some released facts is one thing, wild baseless conjecture is another. The vast majority of us (anyone NOT a playtester) have no idea how the actual mechanics for the new combat system works, let alone how specific splats may change those effects. Sorry I know that was a tangent there, but the constant &quot;I think 3E (insert splat here) are gonna work like this,&quot; is really starting to get old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T22:08:08-07:00","id":154521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=154506#post154506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry I know that was a tangent there, but the constant &quot;I think 3E (insert splat here) are gonna work like this,&quot; is really starting to get old.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we need <i>something</i> to talk about in the weeks, months and years it will be before 3e comes out and the appropriate splat books are released.<br /> <br /> And I'm no where near drunk enough to start &quot;The Vision of Bronze: Good Idea or Best Idea?&quot; yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T22:08:37-07:00","id":154522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=154506#post154506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and No! Even the current 3E designers have said that the &quot;story of Exalted is the return of the Solars&quot;. Now just because that's the big schtick of the story, doesn't mean you shouldn't be able to play other Exalted though. The game has allow play of many types (mortal, terrestrial, raksha, celestial exalts, etc) since 1st edition. There's absolutely no reason, and no intent by the current designers to change that. As for Sidereals, they may need a bit more ST assistance then others. But their Astrology exists for that very reason. It gives them a way of tapping into the ST and pulling tid bits of info from the source. While I've never cared much for Sidereals myself, I always thought clever uses of astrology were some of the most interesting reasons to play a Sidereal.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I think people just need to wait for their 3E splat book. Useless speculation on Sidereals, Lunars, Infernals, or whatever really, is pointless. Outside of the designers themselves, none of us know how things will change. Speculation based on some released facts is one thing, wild baseless conjecture is another. The vast majority of us (anyone NOT a playtester) have no idea how the actual mechanics for the new combat system works, let alone how specific splats may change those effects. Sorry I know that was a tangent there, but the constant &quot;I think 3E (insert splat here) are gonna work like this,&quot; is really starting to get old.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarification. They said the story of Exalted pivots on the return of the Solars, not that's it's totally about the return of the Solars. Exalted can be just as much about Solars, as a current and developed situation where the wildcard of Solars returning causes the involved parties to rethink and think of new strategies and actions. Not one person can play the Solar, but the story can still involve their return, even as a small detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T06:23:15-07:00","id":155608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=153361#post153361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It might be simpler just to make Sidereals an explicitly ST only territory, rather than a player choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is basically the same argument people make for scrapping Craft, rather than address the decker problem the whole subsystem should be cut and the creation of artifacts left in the hands of dedicated NPCs who never leave their workshops. <br /> Seeing a variation of it coming from you it is hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T15:29:13-07:00","id":156027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=155608#post155608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is basically the same argument people make for scrapping Craft, rather than address the decker problem the whole subsystem should be cut and the creation of artifacts left in the hands of dedicated NPCs who never leave their workshops.<br /> Seeing a variation of it coming from you it is hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kinda part of why I suggest that Sidereals should be able to put a couple of epic twists of fate in their back pocket and save them for later. The idea of Sidereals having this greater perception of the world and the ability to make plans accordingly is great, but if you are playing in a mixed game the GM will often just roll their eyes at you when you suggest using these powers because it can be so out of character with what the other splats are capable of doing. I can see why some people would suggest that Sidereals in some ways work better as NPCs, but I think changes could be made so that instead of being the splat who always has the plan, they could be the splat who always SEEMS to have the plan.<br /> <br /> That's why I like the idea of having these useful and slightly flexible outcomes held in reserve, from the Sidereal's point of view they just know they really need this situation to turn out differently so they change it, from the Solar's point of view it looks as if the Sidereal had a plan all along, and from the GM's point of view they didn't have to share their campaign notes with a player just to make their powers work. Another example I have been thinking of would be the situation where the party is hopelessly lost, the Sidereal could use an instance of &quot;Hidden Path Revealed&quot; they had motes committed to and suddenly they have inserted a fate into reality where they know of a secret trail around the corner that will get them to where they need to go. The sidereal is relieved that they spent the motes on that snippet of fate a couple months ago, and the rest of the party is amazed at this mysterious Sidereal who always seems to know more than they should.<br /> <br /> If there were one or two of these sort of &quot;emergency charms&quot; in each charm tree I think the Sidereal's could have a play-style somewhere in between &quot;Prepared for every outcome&quot; and &quot;It's uncanny how things always work out for them&quot; without them becoming the spat with metagaming built right in.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T02:13:09-07:00","id":156323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=155608#post155608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is basically the same argument people make for scrapping Craft, rather than address the decker problem the whole subsystem should be cut and the creation of artifacts left in the hands of dedicated NPCs who never leave their workshops.<br /> Seeing a variation of it coming from you it is hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must admit that I don't see how the sidereal problem = craft problems. Though to be fair I tend to call the entire notion of Craft issues = decker to be BS and often feel that the rules are rather too convoluted for most people to easily grasp and then optimize so the games run smoothly.<br /> <br /> I have run many crafting characters as both a Player and been STing with Crafters in the group and almost every single one was mobile and didn't slow the groups down in the slightest. This is by definition not the problem referred to as a &quot;Decker Problem&quot;.<br /> <br /> I will admit that a Crafter has to be properly setup at Character Gen. to allow them to function and not slow the group down, but that is a one time concession to the player of the character. A Prepared Caster (specifically a sidereal) on the other hand is some one who would need that special concession in nearly every encounter.<br /> <br /> Exalted is a complex system and trying to build a PC class that revolves around constantly having quasi-ST level intel at all times just feels very inelegant as far as keeping things running smoothly is concerned. If anything it tends to invite power creep issues.<br /> <br /> I advocated the Sidereals removal because if you simply take away the whole Fate schtick, then they really don't have anything they can call their own other than SMA, which is a separate discussion in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T07:54:10-07:00","id":156519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=156323#post156323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I must admit that I don't see how the sidereal problem = craft problems. Though to be fair I tend to call the entire notion of Craft issues = decker to be BS and often feel that the rules are rather too convoluted for most people to easily grasp and then optimize so the games run smoothly. I have run many crafting characters as both a Player and been STing with Crafters in the group and almost every single one was mobile and didn't slow the groups down in the slightest. This is by definition not the problem referred to as a &amp;quot;Decker Problem&amp;quot;. I will admit that a Crafter has to be properly setup at Character Gen. to allow them to function and not slow the group down, but that is a one time concession to the player of the character. A Prepared Caster (specifically a sidereal) on the other hand is some one who would need that special concession in nearly every encounter. Exalted is a complex system and trying to build a PC class that revolves around constantly having quasi-ST level intel at all times just feels very inelegant as far as keeping things running smoothly is concerned. If anything it tends to invite power creep issues. I advocated the Sidereals removal because if you simply take away the whole Fate schtick, then they really don't have anything they can call their own other than SMA, which is a separate discussion in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div> Calling them prepared casters was probably stupid on my part. Im not suggesting that they get special insider knowledge on the story, but rather that they can hold in reserve favourable twists of fate that can be applied to a band of situations. Like a snippet of good luck that can only be applied to a limited band of survival situations that could crop up. So rather than actually having a elaborate plan based on knowledge of fate, they can twist fate just to make it look like they do!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T09:05:41-07:00","id":156579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=156519#post156519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Calling them prepared casters was probably stupid on my part. Im not suggesting that they get special insider knowledge on the story, but rather that they can hold in reserve favourable twists of fate that can be applied to a band of situations. Like a snippet of good luck that can only be applied to a limited band of survival situations that could crop up. So rather than actually having a elaborate plan based on knowledge of fate, they can twist fate just to make it look like they do!</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like they already have that, in many of their Charms and Resplendencies. With the former they don't have to &quot;store them up&quot;, but that also means they are better able to &quot;fake&quot; having had a plan. The latter are basically as you describe, though because Sidereals, you get whatever effects the College comes with, and some are more &quot;favorable twist of fate&quot;-ish than others. For example, there's one in The Mast (I think) that boosts your Strength for the purposes of teamwork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 06-02-2014, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T21:41:37-07:00","id":157461,"title":"","content":"Wow, I must have stepped through a time portal and skipped like a year of conversation. Just a month ago people were telling me how Sidereals couldn't come out soon enough, now it's &quot;the Sidereal problem&quot; and &quot;we should remove them as PCs.&quot; What is &quot;the problem&quot; and why is that a solution? I need to know for science purposes; I need to understand why the conversation is shifting this way in random threads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T21:55:33-07:00","id":157470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157461#post157461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I must have stepped through a time portal and skipped like a year of conversation. Just a month ago people were telling me how Sidereals couldn't come out soon enough, now it's &quot;the Sidereal problem&quot; and &quot;we should remove them as PCs.&quot; What is &quot;the problem&quot; and why is that a solution? I need to know for science purposes; I need to understand why the conversation is shifting this way in random threads.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't really know where that came from...I started the thread to talk about what I thought could be a cool style of charms for sidereal's but things seem to have gone off the rails as they are wont to do. I just wanted a way to have Sidereals seem like the all-knowing, always prepared character even if they are just channeling the idea of, fake it till you make it, with a little essence on top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T22:01:59-07:00","id":157485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157461#post157461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I must have stepped through a time portal and skipped like a year of conversation. Just a month ago people were telling me how Sidereals couldn't come out soon enough, now it's &quot;the Sidereal problem&quot; and &quot;we should remove them as PCs.&quot; What is &quot;the problem&quot; and why is that a solution? I need to know for science purposes; I need to understand why the conversation is shifting this way in random threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Drunken Pattern Spiders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T22:09:13-07:00","id":157492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d#post153267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This concept came up in a discussion about how the celestial splats can be balanced against each while still maintaining the concept of Solars being the best at what they do in a very straight forward sense of achievement. We were trying to come up with roundabout ways in which the other splats can work around or, even negate the power a solar gains from just \u201cbeing better\u201d than everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's backwards.<br /> <br /> Sidereals aren't distinct from Solars in order to &quot;let&quot; Solars be the best at what they do, or to find ways to sneak around and beat Solars anyway.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are what they are in order to be Sidereals, which includes being meaningfully distinct from other splats (including Solars.)<br /> <br /> There's a host of implications stemming from what Solars are and what they do, or from the fact that Exalted is a game and therefore requires some degree of balance; but using those implications to inform core Sidereals powers is putting the cart before the horse. Decide what Sidereals should be and get a general concept for how they'll work mechanically, <i>then</i> figure out how you'll balance that into the game.<br /> <br /> Or, in other words -- when you're designing a splat, you start with some basic concepts about how they'll work and what their charms will do, then you implement those with an eye towards overarching balance and how they interact with other splats. If you can't resolve it, you go back to the drawing board; and obviously your basic concept needs to be meaningfully distinct as a whole; but if you start with the presumption of &quot;how can I avoid stepping on these people's toes, while still beating them&quot; you will end up with awkwardly-designed splats that will feel like they're assembled out of other people's scraps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T22:10:34-07:00","id":157493,"title":"","content":"People going stir crazy waiting for their favorite splat and discussing stereotypes that they agree/disagree with.<br /> <br /> Personally, I've always seen Sidereals as a cross between the FBI/KGB + James Bond gadgetry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 06-03-2014, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T22:20:11-07:00","id":157521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157492#post157492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's backwards.<br /> <br /> Sidereals aren't distinct from Solars in order to &quot;let&quot; Solars be the best at what they do, or to find ways to sneak around and beat Solars anyway.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are what they are in order to be Sidereals, which includes being meaningfully distinct from other splats (including Solars.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's kinda what we were talking about though, coming up with something uniquely Sidereal that lets them be competitive in a game where the the absolute rule is that in any straight forward competition the Solar is gonna win. I don't think coming up with a mechanic that is specially the Sidereal's, and coming up with a mechanic that balances them against the Solars, need to be mutually exclusive parts of their design. One mechanic can be both things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T23:07:03-07:00","id":157551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157521#post157521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's kinda what we were talking about though, coming up with something uniquely Sidereal that lets them be competitive in a game where the the absolute rule is that in any straight forward competition the Solar is gonna win. I don't think coming up with a mechanic that is specially the Sidereal's, and coming up with a mechanic that balances them against the Solars, need to be mutually exclusive parts of their design. One mechanic can be both things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;balance them against the Solars&quot; please? You mean abilities that let them manipulate Fate, they have that. The ability to be martial arts masters, Sidereal Martial Arts much! Abilities that allow them to act as agents of Heaven, Resplendent Destinies and access to Yu Shan Bureaucracy. They have everything they're suppose to have, the issue with 2E was that it was a copy-paste job from 1E and most of there abilities didn't work like they were intended to in the new edition. That will likely get fix in 3E. So what specifically are you asking for here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T23:21:32-07:00","id":157561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157551#post157551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Define &quot;balance them against the Solars&quot; please? You mean abilities that let them manipulate Fate, they have that. The ability to be martial arts masters, Sidereal Martial Arts much! Abilities that allow them to act as agents of Heaven, Resplendent Destinies and access to Yu Shan Bureaucracy. They have everything they're suppose to have, the issue with 2E was that it was a copy-paste job from 1E and most of there abilities didn't work like they were intended to in the new edition. That will likely get fix in 3E. So what specifically are you asking for here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok so I just want to make this clear I made this thread to see what people thought of an idea I had for a take on Sidereal charms. The whole balancing them against Solars thing was secondary to what I thought might be a neat style of charms. And yes Sidereals already have abilities that manipulate fate and resplendent destinies, and both those things if done well could give them some balance against a solar while not infringing on Solars territory of being the most skilled in a straight forward way. What I described in my initial post was just what I thought might be a new take on those same Sidereal themes, in a style that could help to bring the splats closer to parity. I kinda feel like you are taking umbrage with me after reading my response to a post that already was putting word in my mouth in the first place, I'm not sure what part of my comments offend you....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T00:09:28-07:00","id":157589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157461#post157461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I must have stepped through a time portal and skipped like a year of conversation. Just a month ago people were telling me how Sidereals couldn't come out soon enough, now it's &quot;the Sidereal problem&quot; and &quot;we should remove them as PCs.&quot; What is &quot;the problem&quot; and why is that a solution? I need to know for science purposes; I need to understand why the conversation is shifting this way in random threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that we have different versions of sidereals. The whole they have to prepare in advanced to be successful part that they've always had mentioned but never really dealt with. Personally my issue with this has to be astrology. Resplendencies which are destiny powers that have to be made in advanced that should be stronger and grow with colleges rather than stay as stagnet minor powers. Allowing an astrologer the ability to prepare powers in advanced like an alchemical rather than fast cast MA which be a nice addition for sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 06-03-2014, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T04:53:37-07:00","id":157723,"title":"","content":"Preptime is nice as far as it goes, but you don't want to overly focus a splat on preptime or it makes them unpleasant to play (see, for instance, the 15-minute working day in D&amp;D), and it pushes the game toward something closer to modern war, where there's a lot of tedious set-up and double-checks, and actual conflict is usually sudden, brutal, and one-sided. SIdereals as &quot;preptime Exalted&quot; is fine when it's a matter of making sure that some of their key effects are only accessible via weird shenanigans like Earth and Sky Bargain, but trying to expand astrology heavily into that role would, I think, have deleterious effects on the splat. You don't want to overly incentivize the Sidereal to noodle around in Heaven 90% of the time and rely on Scry and Die as a general methodology, because although Sidereals are &quot;NPC-flavoured&quot;, they are a PC splat, and they're a lot more interesting as a PC splat than they would be as pure NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T05:00:44-07:00","id":157725,"title":"","content":"From what I can tell, &quot;prep time&quot; for Sidereals has generally amounted to stocking up on prayer strips, and a number of Charms that have certain context dependencies that they get stronger benefits from if they work to control them, which is often aided particularly by their more direct Charms, and some of the astrology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T05:25:45-07:00","id":157736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157461#post157461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I must have stepped through a time portal and skipped like a year of conversation. Just a month ago people were telling me how Sidereals couldn't come out soon enough, now it's &quot;the Sidereal problem&quot; and &quot;we should remove them as PCs.&quot; What is &quot;the problem&quot; and why is that a solution? I need to know for science purposes; I need to understand why the conversation is shifting this way in random threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is basically Meme!Sidereals, invariably elder Exalts who are permanently one step ahead of the PCs, appear on-screen to Avoidance Kata away and whose entire existence revolves around Faction politics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T05:27:50-07:00","id":157738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157461#post157461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I must have stepped through a time portal and skipped like a year of conversation. Just a month ago people were telling me how Sidereals couldn't come out soon enough, now it's &quot;the Sidereal problem&quot; and &quot;we should remove them as PCs.&quot; What is &quot;the problem&quot; and why is that a solution? I need to know for science purposes; I need to understand why the conversation is shifting this way in random threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, John, people have been considering the removal of Sidereals since roughly forever. The whole &quot;Sidereals were not really originally thought as a PC splat and it shows like hell&quot; (with the people saying this split between finishing that sentence with &quot;so we must fix them&quot; and &quot;so they should be removed as a PC splat) has been an ongoing line of discussion for <i>years</i>. I barely pay attention to this game and even I know this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T06:04:57-07:00","id":157753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157738#post157738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, John, people have been considering the removal of Sidereals since roughly forever. The whole &quot;Sidereals were not really originally thought as a PC splat and it shows like hell&quot; (with the people saying this split between finishing that sentence with &quot;so we must fix them&quot; and &quot;so they should be removed as a PC splat) has been an ongoing line of discussion for <i>years</i>. I barely pay attention to this game and even I know this!</div> </div> </div> </div>I never understood the argument that they weren't intended to be a PC splat. I get that much of their charms and the things they do are just not fun to play with and should probably be changed, but given that Exalted was supposed to be a prequel to classic WOD and the Sidereals are meant to be the mage analogs, they should totally be PCs.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T08:28:52-07:00","id":157867,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if anything, they have the opposite problem -- Sidereals have traditionally had a huge number of charms that are fine when used by PCs, but cause problems when used by NPCs. (Transcendent Hatchet of Fate, Of Things Desired and Feared, Five Ordeals Odyssey, Shun the Smiling Maiden, etc.) -- charms that operate on a narrative fiat level that works fine for PCs and has enough restrictions so it doesn't break the game when they're the ones using it, but which is generally not fun when it's being used against you. One symptom of this is that Sidereals (especially in 1e, where they were otherwise well-designed) had a ton of charms with no clear way to defend against them.<br /> <br /> The 2e Sidereal Astrology section straight-up says &quot;do not actually use this for NPCs; just pretend you did.&quot; (Not that 2e Sidereal Astrology was very fun for PCs using it, either; but that illustrates the problem. It is fun to weave the fates of others, but much less fun to feel that your own fate is being weaved by a distant NPC.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-03-2014, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:15:23-07:00","id":157920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157738#post157738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, John, people have been considering the removal of Sidereals since roughly forever. The whole &quot;Sidereals were not really originally thought as a PC splat and it shows like hell&quot; (with the people saying this split between finishing that sentence with &quot;so we must fix them&quot; and &quot;so they should be removed as a PC splat) has been an ongoing line of discussion for <i>years</i>. I barely pay attention to this game and even I know this!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals are a PC splat designed to take a character concept that would normally be a bullshit Mysterious NPC and make them into a playable group. Saying that they shouldn't be playable because they were originally conceived of as NPCs is like saying that Abyssals shouldn't be playable because they were initially conceived of as bad guys -- the &quot;it's like this traditionally non-protagonist character type, but designed to be a protagonist&quot; thing is intrinsic to what makes them cool. FWIW, 1e Sidereals pulled this off better than 1e <i>or</i> 2e Abyssals.<br /> <br /> It's important to recognize that Sidereals are not simply an NPC class made playable, they're a detailed investigation of what an NPC class might look like from the inside, if it were meant to be functional as a PC class, either in a mixed group or a group of all that type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:58:55-07:00","id":157980,"title":"","content":"The only thing I want to know about Ex3 Sidereals is: will the Infinite Resplendence Amulet return?<br /> <br /> Because that is my very favoritest Artifact for sids. Being able to change disguise instantly (or just make sure you're wearing the latest fashion at all times)? Stealthy MA-compatible armor? The ability to pull all kinds of stuff out of my sleeves, including prayer strips, a calligraphy brush and some ink, an umbrella, a rose, enough cash to buy a village twice over, long strips of clothes I can walk on using Crane Form all wuxia-style, and a literal <i>ton</i> of throwing daggers, swords, kusarigama, cast iron skillets and other assorted weapons? Best. Thing. Ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T12:38:26-07:00","id":158109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157980#post157980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I want to know about Ex3 Sidereals is: will the Infinite Resplendence Amulet return? Because that is my very favoritest Artifact for sids. Being able to change disguise instantly (or just make sure you're wearing the latest fashion at all times)? Stealthy MA-compatible armor? The ability to pull all kinds of stuff out of my sleeves, including prayer strips, a calligraphy brush and some ink, an umbrella, a rose, enough cash to buy a village twice over, long strips of clothes I can walk on using Crane Form all wuxia-style, and a literal <i>ton</i> of throwing daggers, swords, kusarigama, cast iron skillets and other assorted weapons? Best. Thing. Ever.</div> </div> </div> </div> Haha so cool! Sounds like a wearable TARDIS, full of odds and ends, and every costume imaginable!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T13:07:32-07:00","id":158181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=158109#post158109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Haha so cool! Sounds like a wearable TARDIS, full of odds and ends, and every costume imaginable!</div> </div> </div> </div>They were one of the very few things that came out of the Dreams of the First Age box set that didn't cause the setting to implode or break half the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T13:40:32-07:00","id":158224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157753#post157753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I never understood the argument that they weren't intended to be a PC splat. I get that much of their charms and the things they do are just not fun to play with and should probably be changed, but given that Exalted was supposed to be a prequel to classic WOD and the Sidereals are meant to be the mage analogs, they should totally be PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div> The problem is one of execution, rather than intent.<br /> <br /> Sidereals were supposed to be the Mage analog, but the &quot;best&quot; sorcerers in the game are the Solars (the Hunter analog for some reason), this left the MA connection of &quot;Do&quot; from the Mage system which becomes the fluff basis for all the SMA.<br /> <br /> Essentially Sidereals are bits and pieces of &quot;cool concepts&quot; that didn't add up to much on their own, but when lumped together almost make a functional splat. It just also happens that most of those bits and pieces tend to be the exact same qualities which are normally associated with NPCs, specifically ST-NPCs which are always one step ahead, always have foreknowledge and always have a plan.<br /> <br /> Never mind the fact that the spiritual enlightenment of MA, the tough as nails CIA spook and divine cubicle worker shticks don't mesh well on any level. Basically they are an ST NPC race that can fit a broad range of rolls, rather than a PC race that can be played in different ways.<br /> <br /> Each splat can be broken down into some core concepts, some mechanical, some fluff and finally some storyline based which make up the feel and direction of said splat.<br /> <br /> In the case of Sidereals they have the following:<br /> <br /> <b>Fate &amp; Astrology:</b><br /> As a replacement for total mastery of Sorcery, the Sidereals have control of fate. But if you think about it, the very notion of being exalted is all about carving out your own fate. Of over coming the situation by your own will and changing the course of history. Thus Fate becomes a paradoxical concept that controls everything in the setting and nothing at the same time. Does anyone really feel like the Fate powers are on par with Sorcery in Exalted, to make up for the fact that the Mage analogs are worse at magic use than the hunter analogs?<br /> <br /> <b>Xanatos Manipulation:</b><br /> With the aforementioned control and foreknowledge of Fate comes not just the ability, but in many cases the expectation of Xanatos level manipulations to steer the course of the situation in games. But since all the important characters (PCs and high end NPCs) are either outside of Fate or have the power level to simply change the course of history via their actions, then it is not believable to say that Sidereals can actually control Fate. This conclusion then undermines the first concept of having control over Fate in the first place. Thus it is a function of the ST saying so, rather than a function of the class.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereal Martial Arts:</b><br /> So while all Exalted are by definition an advanced integrated weapons system, how is it that the smallest mote pool Celestial Exalts, who are not regarded as front line warriors or even functional spec-ops combatants, are given the most powerful MA combat charms in the game? The answer is game balance, not because it makes thematic sense or even logistical sense if you think of all the Exalt types forming a cohesive army, which the backstory of their design implies or outright says.<br /> <br /> <b>Trainers and Wise Elders:</b><br /> Currently Dragon-Blooded are better trainers than Sidereals, mechanically speaking. That alone should be enough to say that something has gone horribly wrong. Lastly the whole concept of knowing forgotten knowledge of ages past is not a class specific benefit, but a background perk. If you swapped things around so that the Lunars or Solars ran Yu-Shan rather than being hunted, they would have said knowledge and surviving wise elders. The whole trainers &amp; Elders thing is a fluff contrivance based on the Sidereals being the basis for the Usurpation, just like the good little plot devices/NPCs they truly are.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, I might have to explore this further.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T14:05:12-07:00","id":158263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157738#post157738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, John, people have been considering the removal of Sidereals since roughly forever. The whole &quot;Sidereals were not really originally thought as a PC splat and it shows like hell&quot; (with the people saying this split between finishing that sentence with &quot;so we must fix them&quot; and &quot;so they should be removed as a PC splat) has been an ongoing line of discussion for <i>years</i>. I barely pay attention to this game and even I know this!</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I don't doubt you or anything, Drascin, but I have to admit that <i>I've</i> only ever seen that argument come up in regards to Lunars. Maybe I'm ignoring the wrong threads.<br /> <br /> I have definitely heard the arguments Thoth is advancing, and from people whom I respect as gamers and storytellers- but I've played Sidereals for years now, and my experiences have been pretty good. The mechanics have often failed me, but the thematic mash has usually worked quite well. <br /> <br /> (Mind you, I think part of this is that 'enlightened master' and 'CIA spook' actually do mesh quite well if you recognize that 'cubicle worker' isn't actually a thing Sidereals do. 'Paperwork', as the term gets thrown around, is code for politics... not actual paperwork. You can get out of doing paperwork forever with an Ess 2 charm, man.)<br /> <br /> ((Unless you make the terrible mistake of using the Astrology rules as applied, but I don't think that's enough to sink the splat.))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T21:27:16-07:00","id":159724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=157561#post157561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok so I just want to make this clear I made this thread to see what people thought of an idea I had for a take on Sidereal charms. The whole balancing them against Solars thing was secondary to what I thought might be a neat style of charms. And yes Sidereals already have abilities that manipulate fate and resplendent destinies, and both those things if done well could give them some balance against a solar while not infringing on Solars territory of being the most skilled in a straight forward way. What I described in my initial post was just what I thought might be a new take on those same Sidereal themes, in a style that could help to bring the splats closer to parity. I kinda feel like you are taking umbrage with me after reading my response to a post that already was putting word in my mouth in the first place, I'm not sure what part of my comments offend you....</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure why you'd think I was offended. I'm more just confused by what your asking. From my point of view, the devs are making drastic changes to the game in 3E. Everything will have to change to accommodate these mechanical changes. Asking for new mechanics for Sidereals when in truth, no one knows what the intended mechanics are going to be seems... outright stupid! Hence my confusion by a lot of these &quot;you should make x change to (insert splat here) to make them balanced against (insert another splat here)&quot; forum topics that have been popping up. There was a &quot;change Lunars by doing this&quot; forum last month. It just seems silly to ask for changes when you don't know what's already being changed.<br /> <br /> I still think speculating on changes we know of, have been hinted at, or actual previewed in KS updates is a great way to pass the time. Suggesting changes to splats we know absolutely nothing about mechanics wise, in a new system we know very little about, is kind of a waste of time. I'm done with this thread though, so feel free to have at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T22:13:06-07:00","id":159747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=159724#post159724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure why you'd think I was offended. I'm more just confused by what your asking. From my point of view, the devs are making drastic changes to the game in 3E. Everything will have to change to accommodate these mechanical changes. Asking for new mechanics for Sidereals when in truth, no one knows what the intended mechanics are going to be seems... outright stupid! Hence my confusion by a lot of these &quot;you should make x change to (insert splat here) to make them balanced against (insert another splat here)&quot; forum topics that have been popping up. There was a &quot;change Lunars by doing this&quot; forum last month. It just seems silly to ask for changes when you don't know what's already being changed.<br /> <br /> I still think speculating on changes we know of, have been hinted at, or actual previewed in KS updates is a great way to pass the time. Suggesting changes to splats we know absolutely nothing about mechanics wise, in a new system we know very little about, is kind of a waste of time. I'm done with this thread though, so feel free to have at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say I think it's entirely appropriate to talk about ways in which Solars and the other splats can function with some balance (not outright stupid...), we may not know the exact mechanics of how Solars work in EX3, but we do know that they will continue to be the most directly powerful exalts, and if the other splats are going to be able to be played on equal footing they will need to have systems and options in play that allow them to compete in unique and less direct ways.<br /> <br /> And why can't we ask for or speculate changes? The developers are making this game for us, we are the customers, and I would really hope in, fact I'm sure, they are taking some measure of what we are looking for in Exalted to guide the game in new directions. It doesn't matter to me if what I suggested is something they are planning to do, something that plants a seed of an idea in their minds, or is entirely off base because they are going in a even cooler direction, these are all great outcomes as far as I'm concerned, and a good reason to keep on coming up with new ideas and suggestions!<br /> <br /> If you can't see the fun or purpose in mental exercises and wild speculation than I guess it is probably better that you are &quot;done with this thread&quot; as you put it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T02:16:08-07:00","id":159836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=158224#post158224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sidereals were supposed to be the Mage analog, but the &quot;best&quot; sorcerers in the game are the Solars (the Hunter analog for some reason), this left the MA connection of &quot;Do&quot; from the Mage system which becomes the fluff basis for all the SMA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars may have the potential to be better sorcerers, but Sidereals have more of a &quot;feel&quot; of sorcery running through their general Charm set.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fate &amp; Astrology:</b><br /> As a replacement for total mastery of Sorcery, the Sidereals have control of fate. But if you think about it, the very notion of being exalted is all about carving out your own fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>So making other Exalts follow the script is a noteworthy challenge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Trainers and Wise Elders:</b><br /> Currently Dragon-Blooded are better trainers than Sidereals, mechanically speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>would</i> like it if Sidereals had a few more mechanically expressed effects to train, but I mostly think that Sidereals should have the concept of being a mentor run through the Charms as a whole, coming up in and having applications that one might not expect.<br /> <br /> I feel that it might be a bit more Sidereal-flavoured to have it that being trained by one of their sifus means they can use various effects through you or to influence your life, rather than necessarily training you better than somebody else would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T02:21:12-07:00","id":159838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=159836#post159836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Solars may have the potential to be better sorcerers, but Sidereals have more of a &quot;feel&quot; of sorcery running through their general Charm set.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree and disagree. There are in some ways a better feel in others a worse. A number of charms can feel that way but I find on a whole it's very different than mage even old mage. And Solars are pretty much better sorcerers in every way. They learn it faster, they learn it easier, they hit all the tiers. An elder may have access to more spells but Adamant Counter magic doesn't give a shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T05:52:36-07:00","id":159927,"title":"","content":"since this thread is going in a more general direction that the original subject,I'ld like to express a few elements :<br /> <br /> Although sidereals have themes closer to &quot;sorcery&quot; than solars, i think they don't have to be &quot;better&quot; or more oriented towards sorcery.<br /> The origin of that understanding is that sidereals have effects that impact the world and/or others directly while solars' charms only enhance their own actions and abilities (though those actions in turn can/will affect the people and world around them).<br /> Even their anima extends to others while solar anima powers are personal.<br /> <br /> In the larger scale what I find was detrimental to them was the core ideas concepts defining their charm trees's focus : every charm tree if an ability was not just designed taking in mind what the ability did, but almost exclusively seen from the purview of the maiden associated with it, generally through a subtheme. the end result (just a few exemples) :<br /> - Awareness was almost solely focused towards &quot;endings&quot;, seeing the future, predicting the outcomes of choices etc... leaving them abysmally bad (compared to other splats) for tasks of &quot;pure&quot; awareness. And the pinacle charm in an attack that, unless stunted, doesn't provide any benefit associated with awareness.<br /> <br /> - Lore being designed with secrets in mind, especially if they are horrible and/or destructive, gets charms to learn and wield those secrets in mystic ways... leaving sidereals without powers to help uncover, learn and teach important secrets in a classic way (book reading, training people).<br /> <br /> - Socialize, from the point of view of serenity and with the subtheme of manipulating relationships, gets no charm for reading a social situation and learning the social connexions between peoples. It's a lot harder to get what you want in a social context when you don't know what relations already exist. You could be unknowingly trying to get two enemies to work with each-other and not understand why you fail to get a good result. It's just like a blind man with a big hammer, if he gets lucky and strikes the right place he can do heavy damage, but he has no way to see where is his target.<br /> <br /> - War focuses on patterns, formations and training that enhance the combat capabilities of the mass combat units. But not a single charm that help for the logistic and tactical aspect of mass combat (except recruiting/call for rallying troops).<br /> <br /> <br /> Now it's true it gives an interesting background and &quot;pattern&quot; to their powers. And it fits the fact that the maidens are the ones who designed the charms. Plus the scriptures and the hidden meanings, participate to the mystic feeling associated to sidereals' powers.<br /> <br /> But in the end, keping such a narrow view on their charm design is really detrimental to the end result. Even more than the &quot;closed charmset&quot; clause.<br /> I would find it way more reasonable to do for all the charm trees, just like it was done for a few one (particularly violet bears of sorrows style and the investigation tree) : mix a few charms based on the OTHER maidens into the tree.<br /> <br /> You can put them in an independent tree to keep the &quot;original&quot; one clean. I think it would help a lot to have a few charms show how the maiden of serenity would handle abilities like lore, or medicine. What mercury would do with awareness and war. What the maiden of secrets has to say about linguistics and bureaucracy...<br /> <br /> Don't you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":2172,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","user":"Jack In The Box","date":". 06-05-2014, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T09:37:41-07:00","id":160033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=159927#post159927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can put them in an independent tree to keep the &quot;original&quot; one clean. I think it would help a lot to have a few charms show how the maiden of serenity would handle abilities like lore, or medicine. What mercury would do with awareness and war. What the maiden of secrets has to say about linguistics and bureaucracy...<br /> <br /> Don't you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this idea, and wouldn't be surprised if happens, we already know that the elemental affinities of the DB charms trees will be a little looser with out of aspect charms popping up in trees here and there, the same thing could just as easily happen with the Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T20:07:26-07:00","id":160497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=160033#post160033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like this idea, and wouldn't be surprised if happens, we already know that the elemental affinities of the DB charms trees will be a little looser with out of aspect charms popping up in trees here and there, the same thing could just as easily happen with the Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiplying the Terrestrial Charmset by a factor of five can only be a good thing.<br /> <br /> Conversely, it would remove too many restrictions from the Sidereal Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T20:30:00-07:00","id":160506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=160497#post160497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiplying the Terrestrial Charmset by a factor of five can only be a good thing.<br /> <br /> Conversely, it would remove too many restrictions from the Sidereal Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think it would make each of the Sidereal Castes too broad? What if they went the same direction as Solars and gave each Maiden 7 caste abilities, You could have the standard charm set with 5 major charm trees for each caste, but with the addition of 2 new smaller charm trees for each Maiden that are found under what once would have been out of caste abilities. For example Journeys could have the standard large Resistance, Ride, Sail, Survival, and Thrown charm trees, and two smaller charm trees tucked in beside Serenity's Linguistics charms, and Battle's Athletics charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T21:55:58-07:00","id":160568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=160033#post160033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like this idea, and wouldn't be surprised if happens, we already know that the elemental affinities of the DB charms trees will be a little looser with out of aspect charms popping up in trees here and there, the same thing could just as easily happen with the Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also like this idea a lot. Further, I would love it if each Maiden had their own take on each tree, canonically -- but in each Ability, only two or three trees were canonly specified, with the rest left for each table to design. That would give us homebrewers some room to play without opening the closed Charmset, and leave some expansion room for the future. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T03:57:38-07:00","id":160709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=160497#post160497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiplying the Terrestrial Charmset by a factor of five can only be a good thing.<br /> <br /> Conversely, it would remove too many restrictions from the Sidereal Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you really think sidereals not having a single scenelong charm for boosting &quot;mundane&quot; awareness (meaning not vision of the future) is a coherent and interesting restriction?<br /> <br /> Do you really think a splat strongly associated with themes of spying and covert operations should never have a charm for encrypion or create a secure comunicataion chanel?<br /> <br /> The idea is not to give them 5 full trees for each ability and remove any restriction, but to remove the uncoherent/unfun ones. They will still be unable/very ineficient at converting wyld zones into creation or &quot;cleaning&quot; shadowlands. They still won't have an untimate awareness charm that pierces through any sensory trick, they still won't have holy charms as powerful as solar ones etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T05:35:04-07:00","id":160737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=160709#post160709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do you really think sidereals not having a single scenelong charm for boosting &amp;quot;mundane&amp;quot; awareness (meaning not vision of the future) is a coherent and interesting restriction? Do you really think a splat strongly associated with themes of spying and covert operations should never have a charm for encrypion or create a secure comunicataion chanel?</div> </div> </div> </div> ...yes? The fact that you want a super useful straightforward tool you don't have (but that isn't an outright survival necessity, naturally) me that the closed Charmset is doing it's job. Because Sidereals can do those things, even if they don't have a Charm that is explicitly for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T06:54:13-07:00","id":160763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=160737#post160737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...yes? The fact that you want a super useful straightforward tool you don't have (but that isn't an outright survival necessity, naturally) me that the closed Charmset is doing it's job. Because Sidereals can do those things, even if they don't have a Charm that is explicitly for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may also help if EX3 does what it sounds like it's trying to do. For many, the impression from 2e generally ran, &quot;If you don't have a Charm for X, you're wasting your time with it,&quot; and that hit Sidereals hardest. If EX3 is set up such that doing something without a Charm still feels like a genuine option, hopefully that impression will wither a great deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T07:27:59-07:00","id":160781,"title":"","content":"With what their martial arts can accomplish they never struck me as particularly restricted in the first place. It sometimes seems they can develop charms for any situation as long as the solution involves punching something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T08:38:03-07:00","id":160858,"title":"","content":"If you don't want to use martial arts for your basic competencies you always have excellencies. Want to see farther/better? Awareness excellency! Heal people? Medicine Excellency! And in EX3 they are making it far easier to get excellencies, without making them an xp dump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T08:42:49-07:00","id":160873,"title":"","content":"True. Maybe you do need a charm to do anything properly, (a dubious claim at best) but with excellencies, there is <i>always</i> a charm for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T09:22:39-07:00","id":160894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=160873#post160873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. Maybe you do need a charm to do anything properly, (a dubious claim at best) but with excellencies, there is <i>always</i> a charm for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The playtesters did say that the game was awesome even before adding in charms, no reason that wouldn't apply to sidereals as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T13:35:50-07:00","id":161044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=160737#post160737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...yes? The fact that you want a super useful straightforward tool you don't have (but that isn't an outright survival necessity, naturally) me that the closed Charmset is doing it's job. Because Sidereals can do those things, even if they don't have a Charm that is explicitly for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know what? Let's just remove every sidereal charm that isn't &quot;outright survival necessity&quot; and see what happens :<br /> remove all the charms to turn your pet into a god, after all other splats survive without these kind of charms, so why not?<br /> Remove all pinacle charms because after all they have a lot of prerequisites and starting characters survive without having them, so they are not strictly necessary.<br /> Let's also remove all the scatered charms that help deal with gods and spirits and keep only the ones in occult and bureacracy. They cover all the strictly necessary cases, the rest is just fancy decoration.<br /> <br /> So yes, closed charm set is not the issue. That doesn't mean it's &quot;working as intended&quot;.<br /> Where does &quot;outright survival necessity&quot; starts and where does it end when you are confonting other exalts and transcendent entities?<br /> How coherent this is when you take into account that the sidereals where the EYES of the exalted in the primordial war as they were the only exalts to have access to yu-shan. Do you expect solars build up their plans based on information from extremely ineffichent scouts?<br /> How come ALL other celestials have equivalents of KEEN(SENSE) TECHNIQUE and UNSURPASSED(SENSE) DISCIPLINE? Doesn't it means that to be able to at least compete with them sidereals should have at least one analog charm? Especially since those 2 are not limited by and doesn't affect dice caps (because they add successes) and work incredibly well with 2nd excellencies?<br /> <br /> On top of that KEEN(SENSE) TECHNIQUE adds 2 successes for a scene for 3 motes, when you need to pay 4 motes for every roll with the 2nd excellency, You just can't compare those 2 charms seeing the discrepeancy between them.<br /> <br /> So please, look at the overwhelming power difference between every celestial and sidereals and dare say it is working as intended.<br /> <br /> P.S: Also, awareness was only one exemple. Don't forget the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T14:07:51-07:00","id":161083,"title":"","content":"There isn't really anything to talk about in the context of 2e Sidereals' mechanics. 2e Sidereals were botched worse than any other mechanics in the line, and the errata was just enough of a patch to make them playable (whereas before, the consensus seemed to be that they were pretty well unusable by the book). Every good thing from the 2e Sidereal charmset came from 1e, so if you want to talk about the merits and flaws of Sidereal charms relative to those of other Celestials, you really need to go back to a 1e context.<br /> <br /> Mind, they didn't have an Awareness-booster in 1e, either -- not even an Excellency! -- while Solars still did, but the reason why that's OK requires 1e's context to explain, because 1e was the game where Sidereals actually worked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T14:30:25-07:00","id":161104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=161083#post161083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't really anything to talk about in the context of 2e Sidereals' mechanics. 2e Sidereals were botched worse than any other mechanics in the line, and the errata was just enough of a patch to make them playable (whereas before, the consensus seemed to be that they were pretty well unusable by the book). Every good thing from the 2e Sidereal charmset came from 1e, so if you want to talk about the merits and flaws of Sidereal charms relative to those of other Celestials, you really need to go back to a 1e context.<br /> <br /> Mind, they didn't have an Awareness-booster in 1e, either -- not even an Excellency! -- while Solars still did, but the reason why that's OK requires 1e's context to explain, because 1e was the game where Sidereals actually worked.</div> </div> </div> </div>They had one of the best awareness abilities in the game though to make up for it at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T14:36:05-07:00","id":161136,"title":"","content":"The sidereals didn't scout by standing in creation looking at shit. They went to the loom of fate and tracked everything from there. What, you expected them to have something as straight forward as &quot;I can see better&quot; prana? That's not how they work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T19:07:31-07:00","id":161334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=161136#post161136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sidereals didn't scout by standing in creation looking at shit. They went to the loom of fate and tracked everything from there. What, you expected them to have something as straight forward as &quot;I can see better&quot; prana? That's not how they work.</div> </div> </div> </div>So rather than being in the field, they sit back in the ivory tower office building and then forward the information they have gleaned to those splats that can actually do something with that information. The result of this being that the sidereal experience is essentially a game of &quot;epic&quot; telephone, rather than an experience of being heroes who go out and actually fix the problems.<br /> <br /> They don't work, they middle manage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T19:19:16-07:00","id":161339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=161334#post161334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So rather than being in the field, they sit back in the ivory tower office building and then forward the information they have gleaned to those splats that can actually do something with that information. The result of this being that the sidereal experience is essentially a game of &quot;epic&quot; telephone, rather than an experience of being heroes who go out and actually fix the problems.<br /> <br /> They don't work, they middle manage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not exactly fair. Not being completely straightforward in approach doesn't mean they don't have &quot;action oriented&quot; capabilities. And come on, it's not like Sidereals don't have a source for relatively straightforward combat effects. They <i>invented </i>supernatural Martial Arts (at least, they claim they did); if all you want is Awareness buffs try there first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 06-06-2014, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T19:58:27-07:00","id":161361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/153267-sidereals-as-\u201cprepared-casters\u201d?p=161334#post161334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So rather than being in the field, they sit back in the ivory tower office building and then forward the information they have gleaned to those splats that can actually do something with that information. The result of this being that the sidereal experience is essentially a game of &quot;epic&quot; telephone, rather than an experience of being heroes who go out and actually fix the problems.<br /> <br /> They don't work, they middle manage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about that myself I was talking about supernal awareness. It let you do something no awareness ability lets you do. It lets you understand whats happening in around a place in any given time without having to pay active attention to it and it trumps stealth. It wasn't perfect but compared to what everyone got before second edition it was really good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}